Track 3: The Solder-Stain Sacrament
- Story & Context: We gathered at the center of the atrium to bury the last functional terminal, marking the end of our occupation as the city authorities finally cut the perimeter fence. The kalimbas rang out like funeral bells, their metallic tone echoing off the glass ceiling as we smeared black solder paste on our cheeks in a final, silent pact. No one spoke, but we knew that the memory of the mall would live on as a frequency only we could transmit. "Turn the leaden sky into a glass crown."
